{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>GREAT AND SMALL.</b> Rashi's interpretation: 'great' that defeats the 'small.' That is, you shall not have two weights, one of five-quarters of a litra and the other of three-quarters, even though they are two honest weights when taken separately, because the heart knows that his intention is to take with the large one and return with the small one. This is 'great that defeats the small' — it deprives it of one quarter." "<b>In your pouch.</b> A place for scales."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:15.168358417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}